  "title": "Construct the Rectangle",
  "summary": "Given a rectangular web page's area, design a rectangle with length L and width W such that L * W equals the area, L is greater than or equal to W, and L - W is minimized.",
  "statement": "Given a rectangular web page's area, design a rectangle with length L and width W such that L * W equals the area, L is greater than or equal to W, and L - W is minimized. Return [L, W].",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= area <= 10,000,000. Return positive integer dimensions [L,W] with L*W == area and L >= W.",
    "Among all such factor pairs, minimize L-W. Returning any rectangle with the correct area is not sufficient."
  ],
