  "hints": [
    "The shorter factor cannot exceed the square root of the area.",
    "The largest divisor at or below the square root gives the smallest gap.",
    "Start width=isqrt(area), decrement until it divides area, then return [area//width,width].",
    "Integer square root avoids rounding. Smaller candidate widths force larger lengths and therefore larger gaps."
  ],
  "editorial": "For factor pairs with W <= sqrt(area), increasing W decreases L=area/W and narrows the gap. The first divisor encountered below the integer square root is therefore optimal. The small-input oracle enumerates every positive candidate length and minimizes the gap among all feasible pairs.",
